 * `SCCACHE_ALLOW_INCREMENTAL` set to `1` to allow Rust builds with `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=1`; incremental crates go uncached. See [Rust caveats](Rust.md)
 * `SCCACHE_CONF` configuration file path
 * `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS` base directory (or directories) to strip from paths for cache key computation. This is similar to ccache's `CCACHE_BASEDIR` and enables cache hits across different absolute paths when compiling the same source code. Multiple directories can be separated by `;` on Windows hosts and by `:` on any other operating system. When multiple directories are specified, the longest matching prefix is used. Path matching is **case-insensitive** on Windows and **case-sensitive** on other operating systems. Environment variable takes precedence over file configuration. Only absolute paths are supported; relative paths will cause an error and prevent the server from start.
+* `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_VERBATIM_ENV_DEPS` comma-separated names of variables that a Rust crate reads with `env!` or `option_env!` whose values are hashed without stripping `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS`, e.g. `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR,CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH`. Read from the environment of each compile; empty or not valid UTF-8 means none. Names are case-insensitive on Windows. See [Rust caveats](Rust.md)
+* `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_REMAP_PATHS` set to `true`, `on`, or `1` in the environment of a Rust compile to keep the basedirs out of its outputs with `--remap-path-prefix`. See [Rust caveats](Rust.md)
 * `SCCACHE_CACHED_CONF`
 * `SCCACHE_DIST_CLIENT_CACHE_DIR` distributed toolchain cache directory; overrides `[dist].cache_dir` from the configuration file.
 * `SCCACHE_IDLE_TIMEOUT` how long the local daemon process waits for more client requests before exiting, in seconds. Set to `0` to run sccache permanently
diff --git a/docs/Rust.md b/docs/Rust.md
index 61b17d4..f25d1f7 100644
--- a/docs/Rust.md
+++ b/docs/Rust.md
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ sccache includes support for caching Rust compilation. This includes many caveat
 * `-o file` is not supported.
 * Compilation from stdin is not supported, a source file must be provided.
 * Values from `env!` require Rust >= 1.46 to be tracked in caching.
+* With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS`, the values of variables read with `env!` or `option_env!` are hashed with the basedirs stripped, so a crate that bakes `env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")` into its outputs can get a cache hit from another checkout and use that checkout's path. `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_VERBATIM_ENV_DEPS=CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR,CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH` hashes those values verbatim, so only the crates that read them are cached per checkout. A procedural macro that reads the variable with `std::env::var` is not covered, as rustc does not list it in the dep-info. Listing `OUT_DIR` would stop sharing every crate that `include!`s generated code.
+* With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS`, a hit can restore a crate compiled in another checkout, with that checkout's paths in its metadata and debug info. With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_REMAP_PATHS=1` in the environment of the compile, sccache passes rustc `--remap-path-prefix` so that these outputs are the same in every checkout. Paths under a basedir that holds the working directory become relative to the working directory, so diagnostics still lead to the files, but the compilation directory in the debug info is `.` and a debugger has to be started in the directory cargo ran rustc in. Other paths under a basedir that holds the output directory, such as the `OUT_DIR` of a crates.io dependency, are written under `/sccache/basedir`, which names no local file. A `--remap-path-prefix` of the build's own takes precedence where both match. Such compiles are not distributed.
 * Procedural macros that read files from the filesystem may not be cached properly.
 * A procedural macro is identified by its crate metadata, so a change to native code it links, with no change to its Rust source or dependencies, is not seen.
 * `rustc`'s incremental compilation needs to be disabled. See [The Cargo Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#incremental). sccache exits with an error when `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=1` is set, unless `SCCACHE_ALLOW_INCREMENTAL=1` is set: then only the incremental crates (workspace members and path dependencies) go uncached.
